Titre $Hohenbuehelia with dimidiate fruiting bodies
com$ adapt GF nov 2018
1,0$source : G. Consiglio, L. Setti, R.G. Thorn,*///Persoonia 41, 2018: 202–212 ISSN (Online) 1878-9080
1,0$

1,0 $ Metuloid cystidia lacking in hymenium; pileipellis hyphae with amorphous-globular incrustation and sometimes with fine tapering spines each tipped with a droplet; spores globose or ellipsoid $ Resupinatus (not included here)
1,2 $ Hymenial metuloid cystidia present, either projecting and visible as a frosting under a hand lens or immersed and only visible in microscopic section
2,0 $ Pileus reaching 6 cm, dimidiate-orbicular, pearl grey and covered with a deep tomentum that forms a reticulate pattern of spines. - Ontario and Quebec, south to Costa Rica, Europe $ H. mastrucata
2,3 $ Pileus smaller, or tomentum not forming a reticulum
3,4 $ Pileus usually 2 cm or more broad
3,6 $ Pileus usually less than 1.5 cm broad
4,0 $ Pileipellis with pileogloeosphexes; pileus whitish to grey, pale beige, honey brown, dark brown, sometimes olive brown; spores 6.4-8.0 × 3.7-4.5  µm . - Europe, Asia $ H. atrocoerulea
4,5 $ Pileipellis without pileogloeosphexes; pileus off-white, pale beige to honey brown
5,0 $ Pileus pale beige to honey brown with paler margins, with pale to buffy tomentum toward base; spores 6.6-8.1 × 3.4-4.4  µm . - North America, south to Costa Rica, Europe $ H. grisea
5,0 $ Pileus off-white, with at most fine white tomentum towards base; spores 7.0-8.2 × 3.1-3.7  µm . - Costa Rica $ H. carlothornii
6,7 $ Lamellae white to cream or off-white when mature
6,12 $ Lamellae darker initially or in development
7,0 $ Pileus cupulate, grey-brown to black; lamellae few and distant, pure white; spores allantoid, 7.2-9.3 × 3.1-4.3  µm . - Ontario, Michigan and New York, Europe $ H. cyphelliformis
7,8 $ Pileus dimidiate; lamellae moderately close
8,9 $ Pileus pale, straw-coloured to pearl grey
8,10 $ Pileus darker, blue-grey to black
9,0 $ Pileus straw-coloured or pale beige; basidia usually 4-spored; spores 6.6-8.1 × 3.4-4.4  µm ; small forms previously known as H. approximans $ H. grisea
9,0 $ Pileus pearly grey with deep, translucent gelatinous zone; basidia 2-spored, with clamps; spores 8.1-9.9 × 3.8-4.8  µm . - Newfoundland (Thorn 2014) and Europe $ H. fluxilis*
10,0 $ Pileus blue-grey, with whitish to concolourous tomentum toward base; on wood of deciduous trees; spores 6.4-8.0 × 3.7-4.5  µm . - Europe, Asia $ H. atrocoerulea
10,11 $ Pileus deep brown to black; on wood of conifers (rarely deciduous) trees
11,0 $ Pileus glossy black, with fine white tomentum towards base; spores 7.5-8.8 × 4.7-5.6  µm . - Ontario $ H. algonquinensis
11,0 $ Pileus brown to black, finely frosted or with greyish tomentum towards base; spores 6.9-8.0 × 3.6-4.2  µm . - Alberta and Ontario $ H. Canadensis
12,13 $ Metuloids immersed; pileus cupulate and remaining so
12,14 $ Metuloids projecting; pileus cupulate to dimidiate
13,0 $ Pileus grey-brown to blackish with silvery tomentum; usually on hardwood branches; spores 6.3-7.9 x 3.4-4.5  µm . - Boreal North America and Europe $ H. unguicularis
13,14 $ . Pileus jet black, glossy, with at most scattered fine white wisps; on branches of conifers; spores 6.8-8.6 x 3.1-3.9  µm . - Boreal North America and Europe H. pinacearum
14,0 $ On wood of conifers; pileus blackish with pebbly surface and coarse yellowish to black tomentum towards base; spores 7.4-9.1 x 4.0-5.2  µm . - Alberta and Finland $ H. mustialensis
14,15 $ On wood of deciduous trees; pileus less coarsely tomentose
15,0 $ Both pileus and lamellae black; metuloid cystidia trilayered, with dark brown middle layer as seen in the microscope; spores 6.2-7.7 x 3.7-4.4  µm . - Yukon to Costa Rica, Europe $ Resupinatus niger
15,0 $ Pileus dark greyish brown, finely white-tomentose towards base; lamellae at first creamy white then greyish brown; spores 6-8 x 3.2-4.4  µm . - Ontario and Wyoming $ H. nimueae

